"change, or \"not seen\"; and what was known when its rule was chosen, when the KB records it),",
"Formal (a theorem and its statement, or a model and its property; or None), Residual (what could",
"still show the work wrong, and that nobody tested, in three lists. Wanted: each default that no",
"human answered, and each current hypothesis that an agent wrote and no human adopted. Happens:",
"each premise that nobody checked, and each current claim with no check. Follows: each formal",
"statement that is stated and not proved), Disclosures, Waivers (build), Open, To land.",
"With the discovery module it drafts the discovery report too: System (what the system showed) and",
"Findings (each marked as from the system or from a model only) before Claims; Scope, Risk and",
"Not explored after Formal (also without the module, when the KB has such facts).",
"With the discovery module, a Vote section comes before To land. It shows the agent's vote",
"and the formal artifacts' vote only after the human votes in the current round.",
"Fill in Delivered and To land yourself. Check Signals: a signal with no record says no.",
"",
"The text is plain Markdown. Each section has a heading (# Claims:) and a blank line after it.",
"Each item is a bullet, with two more spaces for each level. The label is in **bold**.",
"A claim that needs attention (under, a waiver, a burn that is not proved, a flare, a check that did not",
"pass) puts its status, burn, flare, and checks in nested bullets. A fulfilled claim with nothing to add",
"stays on one line, when the line fits in 100 columns. Long lines are not wrapped.",
"",
"--html FILE also writes the report as one page for a human to review in a browser.",
"The text on stdout does not change. The page works offline. It shows the open items first,",
"then each claim with its status, its checks (latest run and log), and its evidence.",
"The reviewer marks items ok, doubt, or wrong, with a note, and copies the marks as text",
"to paste back to you, such as: c1: doubt - the example does not cover X.",
"--open opens the page with xdg-open (or open). Without --open, nothing opens."
]).
help_lines(doctor, [
"orbit-kb doctor",
"",
"Check swipl and the library. Then run known-answer self-tests on the engine, as a query runs:",
"not with a helper rule, and not under(_), are false when under(a) holds;",
"arithmetic under not gives exactly k2, k3, k4;",
"E18 flags p :- not q, q :- not p; E17 flags -p(b).",
"Exit 2 if something is missing or a self-test fails."
]).
help_lines('model-run', [
"orbit model-run MODEL [--tool z3|cvc5|tlc] [--timeout SECONDS] [--spec FILE] [--cfg FILE] [--with FILE]...",
"",
"Run the solver or the model checker of a model yourself, and record the run. MODEL is a subject with",
"model(MODEL, smt) or model(MODEL, tla). An smt model runs on z3 (else cvc5). A tla model runs on tlc in a",
"temporary directory (nothing is left in the KB): --spec FILE is a harness module that TLC checks (it extends the",
"model), --cfg FILE its config (default: the .cfg of the same name beside the spec), --with FILE a module that",
"the spec extends. The output is runs/N-MODEL.log, kept as the subject MODEL_runN; its first line names the tool, the",
"exit code, the verdict and the digest of each file that took part. When the tool decides (z3 or cvc5: exit 0 and",
"only sat or only unsat; TLC: exit 0 and No error has been found, or exit 11, 12 or 13 and a violation line),",
"model_run(LOG, MODEL, DIGEST) is written and the exit code is 0 (a deadlock, exit 11, is a result: a counterexample). Anything else (unknown, a failing exit, a",
"timeout, a missing tool) keeps the log, writes no model_run and exits 2: it counts for or against no claim.",
"orbit add refuses a model_run fact typed by hand. orbit subject does not refresh the digest of such a log.",
"Each file besides the model file that a run read (--spec, --cfg, --with) is a subject (MODEL_STEM), and the run gets",
"model_run_file(LOG, FILE, DIGEST) for it: when a digest of such a file changes (orbit subject), the run is stale. A run is",
"refused while one of its files differs from its subject (refresh it with orbit subject first).",
"Takes the writer lock."
]).
